From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: close the image file and directory after starting a Unix program

Purpose: a process that starts Unix programs (xptray's volume check every
2 s, the Start menu's Linux launchers) does not gather open files.
Windows behavior: CreateProcess keeps no handle to the image or the
current directory after it returns.
Wine before: when NtCreateUserProcess runs a Unix executable with
fork_and_exec, it returned at once and skipped the cleanup at "done":
the image's file handle and the current directory's Unix fd stayed open.
Each start leaked a handle and two fds in the caller and an open file in
the wineserver. On the EeePC, after two days, xptray held 6224 fds (3096
of /usr/bin/env, 3099 of its current directory), growing by one a
second, and the wineserver 3567.
Change: the Unix program path also leaves through "done".
Scope: all programs; only starting a Unix executable changes.
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/process.c | 4 +---
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/process.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/process.c
index 4c2e7eb..1348ffc 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/process.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/process.c
@@ -764,9 +764,7 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtCreateUserProcess( HANDLE *process_handle_ptr, HANDLE *thread_
         {
             *process_handle_ptr = *thread_handle_ptr = 0;
             memset( info, 0, sizeof(*info) );
-            free( unix_name );
-            free( nt_name.Buffer );
-            return STATUS_SUCCESS;
+            status = STATUS_SUCCESS;
         }
         goto done;
     }
